            <ArticleTitle>Headaches in cervical artery dissections.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Internal carotid artery (ICA) and vertebral artery (VA) dissections are among the common causes of stroke in middle-aged and young adults. The spectrum of clinical presentations of these dissections is broad. Many patients, especially those with ICA dissections, may never develop a stroke.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
